{"name":"Dawn Patrol","hex":"#fedfdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dawn patrol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of going out for a surf at dawn.","The surfers who go out to surf at dawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn_patrol"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Dawn Patrol (1930 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Dawn Patrol is a 1930 American pre-Code World War I film starring Richard Barthelmess and Douglas Fairbanks Jr. It was directed by Howard Hawks, a former World War I flight instructor, who even flew in the film as a German pilot in an uncredited role. The Dawn Patrol won the Academy Award for Best Story for John Monk Saunders, an American writer said to have been haunted by his inability to get into combat as a flyer with the U.S. Air Service. It was subsequently remade in 1938 with the same title, and the original was then renamed Flight Commander and released later as part of the Warner Bros. film catalog."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Dawn-Patrol-1930-Poster.jpg/330px-Dawn-Patrol-1930-Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dawn_Patrol_(1930_film)"},{"title":"The Dawn Patrol (1938 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Dawn Patrol is a 1938 American war film, a remake of the pre-Code 1930 film of the same title. Both were based on the short story \"The Flight Commander\" by John Monk Saunders, an American writer said to have been haunted by his inability to get into combat as a flyer with the U.S. Air Service."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/The_Dawn_Patrol_1938_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dawn_Patrol_(1938_film)"},{"title":"Dawn Patrol (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn Patrol is the debut studio album by American hard rock band Night Ranger, released in November 1982 by Neil Bogart's The Boardwalk Entertainment Co. The cover art of the album features dishes of the Very Large Array in central New Mexico."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/Dawnpnightranger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn_Patrol_(album)"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/The_dawn_patrol.jpg/330px-The_dawn_patrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/The_dawn_patrol.jpg/330px-The_dawn_patrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Left to right: Douglas Fairbanks Jr., Richard Barthelmess and Gardner James","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_dawn_patrol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Explosion_%28The_Dawn_Patrol%29.jpg/330px-Explosion_%28The_Dawn_Patrol%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/Explosion_%28The_Dawn_Patrol%29.jpg/330px-Explosion_%28The_Dawn_Patrol%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The aerial sequences from The Dawn Patrol had a remarkably long lifespan, appearing not only in The Dawn Patrol (1938) but also in British Intelligence (1940).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AExplosion_(The_Dawn_Patrol).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/1280px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn at La Silla Observatory, Chile[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/1280px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn over Serra dos Órgãos National Park, Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/60px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/120px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA